The 10 per cent of workers in the Estonian ICT sector will be paid less than their colleagues
Details of human resources search firm Fontes reveal that 10 per cent of employees in the Estonian ICT sector are getting paid less.
The 10 per cent pay gap exists between male and female, the website Geenius reports.
59 IT and telecommunications companies took part in the Fontes ICT sector pay survey.
A total of 8,577 positions were examined.
63% of the positions were employed by men.
"Although only three companies said the pay gap is in favour of men and the lack of a pay gap for the rest of the companies, in reality, compared to similar jobs, men's monthly base wages are, on average, 10% higher than those of women and the total annual salary for men is 8% higher than that of women on average," Fontes an analyst Weather North said.
